<title>UK: EU budget discipline compatible with jobs - Brown.</title>
<headline>EU budget discipline compatible with jobs - Brown.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said European Union countries could combine budget discipline with new ways of creating jobs.</p>
<p>In an interview with BBC radio from Luxembourg, where he was attending a meeting of EU finance ministers, he said sustainable convergence among EU countries was &quot;absolutely central&quot;,but added:</p>
<p>&quot;You can combine the budget discipline that is absolutely essential for European countries as well as for the European Union...with new ways of creating job opportunities.&quot;</p>
<p>Brown said the European Union should look at new ways of dealing with unemployment and low growth, but he was not proposing any big increases in the EU budget.</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
